course: dictionary
lesson: 15633
title: Tenement: a building full of homes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can be made of clues you already know. Look at the words around it. «The tenement had six floors and twelve flats, all joined by one stair.» Floors and flats are clues: a tenement is a tall building with many homes inside it.
explain: «In the past, tenements in big cities were crowded, and many families shared one toilet.» Crowded and shared are clues that tell you tenements were full of people, and that life in them was often hard. Always ask: what does this word tell me about the building?
explain: Some words mean different things in different places. «In Glasgow, our tenement has a shared stair, called a close, that leads up to our flat.» In Scotland, a tenement can be any block of flats with a shared stair. Context tells you which meaning the writer means.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Tenement» means a large old building divided into many flats.
fact: In the past, some tenements in cities like Glasgow, Edinburgh, Dublin and New York were crowded and often poor.
fact: In Scotland, a «tenement» can be any block of flats several floors high, with a shared stair called a «close».
fact: Today, many people in Scotland still live happily in old stone tenements.
exercise: «The tenement had six floors and twelve flats.» What is a tenement? | A small house with one garden | A shop with a big window | A park with benches | *A large old building divided into many flats
exercise: Jamal says a tenement is a castle. What is the best reason he is wrong? | *It is divided into many flats for different families | It is painted blue | It has a garden | It has a moat
exercise: «Every flat in the tenement had a kitchen and a bedroom.» Find and copy one word that means a home inside a building. | *flat | every | bedroom | kitchen
test: «In the past, tenements were often crowded and poor.» What does crowded mean? | *Full of people with little space | Painted in bright colours | Open to the sea | Empty and quiet
test: «In Scotland, a close is the shared stair inside a tenement.» What is a close? | A small shop | A road between two towns | A front garden with flowers | *A shared stair in a tenement
exam: Lucy reads, «The tenement block was grey, tall and full of families.» What is a tenement? | A type of cake | A tiny tent for camping | A kind of boat | *A block of flats full of families
